    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "a route path, name, methods and requirements live in the arguments of #[Route]; omega-php emits reference.attribute carrying the attribute's name only and publishes no field on any emission, so a Handler is identified by its class and method and not by the URL it serves -- the canonical call view (call.arg0_text and its siblings) that ten Packs now publish is not published by omega-php, and a Symfony route is not a call argument in any case",
      "the template a controller renders is the first argument of $this->render(); omega-php emits call.method named render with no argument text, so SymfonyClass -> Template is unreachable",
      "a Twig reference under the default templates/ root now resolves to the artifact it names, via a data.file join that strips that prefix; a reference into a bundle or a custom Twig namespace (@Admin/list.html.twig, or a root added in twig.yaml) still lands in symfony:template-name:* with no artifact behind it",
      "services.yaml, routes.yaml and framework.yaml are configuration this overlay does not read; omega-yaml publishes a definition.config_key's value as an attribute, which is write-only, so a YAML route could not be linked to the controller it names",
      "container compilation, autowiring resolution and runtime service decoration need runtime state no static fact carries"
